    "probe_text": "The `POST /api/owners` endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:132-318`). Here is everything it does, in execution order.\n\n## Pre-check / authorization\n0. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: the caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role.\n\n## In-order flow inside `addOwner`\n\n1. **Idempotency short-circuit** *(side-effect: read of in-memory map)* \u2014 Reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header. If it is present and was already recorded from a prior successful create, returns the originally-created owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else (no new owner created).\n\n2. **Address normalization** *(side-effect: derives canonical address)* \u2014 Normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Prefers the structured lines when `addressLine1` is present; otherwise falls back to the flat `address` field. Composes `normalizedAddress`.\n\n3. **Required-field validation** \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**) \u2014 Collects any blank fields among `firstName`, `lastName`, the normalized `address` (blank/whitespace-only rejected), `city`, `telephone`, and throws if any are missing.\n\n4. **Future registration-date validation** \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**) \u2014 If a `registrationDate` was supplied and is after `LocalDate.now()` (checked against the raw value, before business-day adjustment), reject.\n\n5. **Effective registration date derivation** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Effective date = supplied date, else today; then rolled forward via `toBusinessDay(...)` past weekends and the fixed 2026 public holidays to the next business day.\n\n6. **Daily create-limit validation** \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**) \u2014 Counts existing owners already carrying that effective (business-day) registration date; if `>= 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`), reject.\n\n7. **Bulk-signup flag derivation** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets a boolean `bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredToday > 80` (`BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`), stored later.\n\n8. **City-capacity validation** \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**) \u2014 Counts owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if `>= 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`), reject.\n\n9. **Postcode validation** \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**) \u2014 Optional. If present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) it must fall in that region's range (2000\u20132099 / 3000\u20133099 / 4000\u20134099). Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode.\n\n10. **Telephone normalization + validation** \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**) \u2014 `toE164(...)`: strips spaces/dashes/brackets, preserves a leading `+`code or assumes `+61` (dropping a single leading `0`), requires `+` followed by 8\u201315 digits, and enforces national-number length for known codes (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210).\n\n11. **Email normalization + validation** \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (**400**) \u2014 Optional. If present, must match the email regex and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`); returned lower-cased. Absent \u2192 `null`.\n\n12. **Household id derivation** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Computes `householdId` = first 12 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode)`. Always computed. Reads the `sharesHousehold` flag.\n\n13. **Identity-duplicate validation** \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**) \u2014 Builds identity key `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` and rejects if any non-deleted existing owner has the same whole key.\n\n14. **Household-duplicate validation** \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (**409**) \u2014 If any non-deleted existing owner already carries this `householdId`, reject \u2014 **unless** `sharesHousehold` is true, which bypasses this check.\n\n--- (past this point the owner is being built and saved) ---\n\n15. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)`.\n\n16. **Set normalized address fields** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Sets `address` = composed normalized address; sets `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` only for structured input (else `null`).\n\n17. **Set normalized telephone** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Stores the E.164 telephone.\n\n18. **Set normalized email** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Stores the lower-cased email (or `null`).\n\n19. **Set household id** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Stores `householdId`.\n\n20. **Set namesake count** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding the new owner.\n\n21. **Set household size** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `householdSize` = existing members with same `householdId` + 1.\n\n22. **Set bulk-signup flag** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Persists the `bulkSignupWarning` computed in step 7.\n\n23. **Set effective registration date** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Stores the business-day-adjusted date from step 5.\n\n24. **Assign customer code** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where REGION comes from postcode range (else city table, else `UNKNOWN`) and HASH8 = first 8 upper-case hex of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`; then de-duplicated by appending `-<n>` (n\u22652) if it collides with an existing code.\n\n25. **Soft-duplicate detection** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Unless `sharesHousehold`, finds the earliest existing owner with same last name + postcode but a different telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (that owner's id, else `null`).\n\n26. **Persist** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` writes the owner (assigning its id).\n\n27. **Map entity \u2192 response DTO** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` (this is where derived read-only fields like `membershipLevel`/`membershipNumber` are computed for the response).\n\n28. **Audit log** *(side-effect)* \u2014 Emits one `AUDIT` info line: owner id, customer code, registration date, membership level, membership number.\n\n29. **Set `Location` header** *(side-effect)* \u2014 `/api/owners/{id}` for the new owner.\n\n30. **Record idempotency key** *(side-effect)* \u2014 If an `Idempotency-Key` header was supplied, stores this response DTO under that key so a repeat returns the same owner.\n\n31. **Return 201 Created** \u2014 Responds with the owner DTO, `Location` header, and **201 CREATED**.\n\nNote: the membership level/number surfaced in the response (steps 27\u201328) are derived inside `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, not in the controller; I can walk through those derivations too if useful."
